.SH NAME
.PP
gemini-markets-auth-login - Authenticate with Gemini via browser


.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBgemini-markets auth login [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Authenticate with Gemini Exchange using OAuth browser login.

.PP
Register your OAuth application with this redirect URL:
  http://localhost:8787/callback

.PP
For a custom Gemini OAuth application, set GEMINI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID and
GEMINI_OAUTH_CALLBACK_PORT if your registered redirect URL uses a
different localhost port. Public PKCE clients do not use a client
secret; set GEMINI_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET only for confidential OAuth apps.
The CLI requests account, balance, history, and order scopes. Those trading
scopes currently cover prediction trading for REST and private WebSocket
operations.


.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for login


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	enable debug logging

.PP
\fB--no-websocket\fP[=false]
	disable WebSocket and use REST API only

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="json"
	output format: json, table, or csv

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress stderr output for pure JSON piping

.PP
\fB--raw\fP[=false]
	output compact JSON without pretty-printing

.PP
\fB--sandbox\fP[=false]
	use sandbox environment

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30
	request timeout in seconds

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	use full field names in JSON output (default: abbreviated)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  export GEMINI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID="your-client-id"
  gemini-markets auth login
  gemini-markets --sandbox auth login
.EE


